{"title":"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Problem_21\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 21</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Problem_22\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 22</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">23</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-24\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">24</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-25\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">25</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Compute the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/9233d045c0f58a0577b52a6d1e280ad6acd254e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\left(\\frac{2}{13}+\\frac{2}{15}\\right)+2\\left(\\frac{5}{13}+\\frac{7}{15}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"234\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18d48e09f54c406c990524304fd9edc5c6b3b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{40}{13}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{72}{65}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{52}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"390\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since Branden Kim is the paragon of all human emotion, he is most resplendent in love and accolades. Who is Branden Kim? For the blind, he is their vision. For the starving, he is their nourishment. For the thirsty, he is their water. For the depressed, he is their happiness. For the oppressed, he is their salvation. He will stand up to fight all injustice. Even though he is only one hundred fifty centimeters tall, he is the champion who blocks all injustice. If Branden Kim has one million fans, I am one of them. If Branden Kim has a hundred fans, I am one of them. If Branden Kim only has one fan, then that is me. If Branden Kim has no fans, I no longer exist. If the world is for Branden Kim, I am for the world. If the world is against Branden Kim, I am against the world. That being said, please, with all due respect, tell me how close the great Branden Kim is to the heavens in meters, assuming the heavens are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> meters off the ground.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/607028bb2437383b4fc0af4d81da7551dd0affa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 850\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 9885\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9985\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 985\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 998.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"474\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>It takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes for Alice to deliver a cake. If Alice needs to deliver <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cakes and she starts delivering cakes at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f20dfdfc254c89ac76fc16cc9a4e1d6da0e5bab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, what time will she finish?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36d24425f7f484dc762c8ea3257823a9a54fe015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1:30\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2:30\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2:50\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3:15\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3:30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"518\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbeb55e9bfc99be9dba97aad59c4cec0eb6c94b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32, 47,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af4b3f8897671e2879b10badf471e5deec8952e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> are divided by a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the remainder is the same for all three divisions. What is the greatest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58b99ef680fcd0b5282df39cde9105e71727e105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 15\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 17\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 22\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Ten logicians are sitting at a table. A server comes and asks if everyone wants coffee. The first logician answers “I don’t know.” Then the second logician answers “I don’t know.” This continues, with each logician answering “I don’t know,” until the tenth logician answers “no, not everyone wants coffee.” How many of the ten logicians want coffee?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89dc6c653d611eb10b27b4e0b58bfe6a3262801d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Alice, Bob, and Charlie are sharing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> identical candies. Because Bob is greedy, he insists that he gets at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> candies. Find the number of ways to distribute the candies.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f762fe0cd657fe3bd51a66a00d6ba0b24c622e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 55\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 66\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 78\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 91\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Bob is advertising the Dallas Reunion Tower by making a poster comparing its height to the Burj Khalifa. Currently, in his diagram, the image of the Burj Khalifa is five times as tall as the Reunion Tower. Bob wants to scale the image of the Reunion tower so that it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870303feff6f491471061a7402eba3e326ba84f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> the height of the Burj Khalifa. If the area of the image of the Reunion tower was originally <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> square inches, what is the area, in square inches, of the scaled image? (Note that scaling is done proportionately in both width and length).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cdd11229f5efc28b57485e07350dea47bec914cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 450\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1000\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2025\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5000\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3b91427c0edd031a15ae287bc8858c4b8ac9afe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020^2 + 2024^2 - 2020 \\cdot 2024 + 2027^2 - 2027(2020 + 2024)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"453\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e295a11704c9beaea01a8f2492cd8602e49fd89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 36\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 37\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 38\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 39\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Nathan and his friends are shopping together for a birthday gift for Nathan’s new girlfriend to celebrate Nathan’s success. For each person he brings along to shop with (including himself), Nathan has to pay an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/6739c8a3ef02d0f557bfbe01c9c92e562ff9a7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> for gas to drive everyone to the shop. The gift that Nathan buys costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6a1da7f18069a90481296d18af7ca979fe3854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, and everybody shopping with him splits the cost of the gift evenly. How many people should Nathan bring with him (excluding himself) to minimize the total cost he needs to pay for the drive and the gift?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a7963579276015fe6bd0337f045c9d028e3d4ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c8889d7ca7a61f9b08535470908e848413f516a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd8754c11b59d41eef1ce5d0e1f2952797e07ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa400aa286e8a1f2443de8669b82bc617fc250ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = 3a_{n-1} - 2a_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Find the largest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />\nsuch that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c5d95df2930f3e5786d760e5dd0c8746efacdb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{100} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887b84d23459beb0583b936101234adb1a01a12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 99\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 100\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>At a school, there exist four student council officers: the president, the vice president, the treasurer, and the secretary. When the officers sit in four chairs in a line, the treasurer and the president cannot sit next to each other, or they will begin to talk and no work will be done. Given this condition, what is the probability the vice president and the president sit next to each other?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb02fa636752c578cd93932b5fb9e3443bbdc53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ce7a1c22387a8a1fd8c4940575545239d92c06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|||||x - 1| - 1| - 1| - 1| - 1| - \\frac{1}{2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"288\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b2493a41ab2f58c1a00f0b14008612ca03e1c78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 12\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given that there is exactly one integer such that fourty-eight multiplied by the square of the reciprocal of the integer added onto the integer itself is equal to seven. Find the number of factors of this integer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc1116155f528990bb014df0135fd364d7d4942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>What is the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> for all triples of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c286a6b2750b9c5c514b55b7f52660b1f66c21f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b &lt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14d493f54ddb319951607a06ffeed3179c21111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{1}{c}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"116\" height=\"37\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567797ed33be3423790ac3b609dc91fe47ec8da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 11\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Shreyan and Kaylee are on opposite vertices of a cube. Each turn, they both randomly move across an adjacent edge to another vertex with equal probability. What is the expected number of turns that occur until the two meet in the middle of an edge for the first time?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e74edb87159f76a2b6d68a94848e90ed145361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 13\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 13.5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 14\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 16\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"411\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> be real numbers which satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa810c880a67bd0b9580f22865a332f24c00166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-48)^2+(y-14)^2=169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"21\" />. What is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/8/ae8e52c9ff91d739a507e91fb1b70c27cf2af9a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"24\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/08670b2184492b4fe128110a472d1b8cf8331e43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 26\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 37\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 50\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 63\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 16\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Alice and Bob are playing a series of games where Alice never has three more wins than Bob and Bob never has three more wins than Alice. Games never end in a draw. The number of ways for them to play <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games such that the series ends in a draw can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fc0aa3438a8d3062a78f453029fecb44b72adb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^xb^y$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are distinct primes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e6cce6d507c7569a1045b6ac295b579b4fbb04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8eec68a816c4e904315b3653d2c0bc3ee47a33b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 15\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 16\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 17\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 18\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/9596b5a2993d0f1ce48e542106bde5b216018861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> be the diameter of a circle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> vary along the circle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all\npossible incenters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a curve missing two points. When the two points are added to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the area enclosed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/484d7088c292065a5bc0b662785432628ffc1e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\pi - b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df6a591474ffd81edd37d8d9f52f6f476caa531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93a482eb3392af1053666f0464bed6b4198818a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 18\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 24\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 27\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 30\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The city of Dallas is issuing new <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit license plates. To make keeping track of different license places easier, each license plate much differ from every other license plate by at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits. For example, the license plates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ae974f902560cea6a89e6e74bf4563bbc89bf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$012345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a0d6eaf0fecc55aab7bfe4976a284a0bda38dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$012344$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> may not both be issued, while the license plates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ae974f902560cea6a89e6e74bf4563bbc89bf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$012345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba05cbf918fb1c7d4ea0cd3debf395d364b37a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$012354$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> may. What is the maximum number of license plates that can be issued?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/7616c3c85b46f876d5fe7346045bd6af8e878162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10,000\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 20,000\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 50,000\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 100,000\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 500,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"591\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 19\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If\n\\begin{align*}\na+8b+27c+64d=2,\\\\\n8a+27b+64c+125d=20,\\\\\n27a+64b+125c+216d=202,\\\\\n64a+125b+216c+343d=2024,\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nthen find the remainder when\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7eb571f24ca8982730b608d9adbc2be1e425ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[125a+216b+343c+512d\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"14\" />\nis divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a82354a17c5cc80b0f94c4f924e658cee5a187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 222\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 242\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 476\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 938\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 962$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 20\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_21\">Problem 21</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 21\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa7e4dae453f67aa78269d730f7cae70296659a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,s,t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" /> are the three solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40b5fba76f8866959763841d9825c9f980744fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-2x^2-3x+5=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/429749dd381e66df42eaed694b9d5d609bcd1590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^4+s^4+t^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/13199dc59cc1358bc93474a011b6c08a6ed00aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 38\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 39\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 40\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 41\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 21\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_22\">Problem 22</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 22\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f7661519159a6678741c369a2e897dfd24579670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=3$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e156331c13aae7e86644da6fa391b4389b826d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> and a right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00322295674c54c5413520f7493470ff32ae3cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4142d351ef99cc26a94e44c1912d904dd4a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> lies inside the triangle and is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00322295674c54c5413520f7493470ff32ae3cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Given that the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4142d351ef99cc26a94e44c1912d904dd4a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0fed14e3ffaed04764cb01b3bd0d1bd38956d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\sqrt{b}-c}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"44\" /> for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and square-free <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, what is the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e947add5766b9f26f6dfe73d9425d87664416459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/3/3330eee7d3a980f0ead177a2f72554046dcd7014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 24\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 25\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 27\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 30\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 22 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>How many positive integers less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7e9a0b98c8c8ca9672004d7d2a0b23784ed4d7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5000$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6cefec3a04b416cc84aaeac20d52c6f76ba7cabc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2+n^8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/089bd9110a94b60c07e5026e79e72a5dca61e9ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 134\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 135\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 136\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 137\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 138$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 23 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people standing in a line, with their heights being some permutation of the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c55c3594a2d350e06f327a506c75f75dc2e7e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,/cdots,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. Some people however, are unhappy because they can’t see the front of the line as there is someone blocking them. As a result, we define the extension needed of each person to be the minimum extra height they would need such that no one in front of them would block them. This is defined independently for each person. Find the expected sum of the extensions needed.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/d/85d847edf5e555e3e4e09f4a1b2ab4d3630e5dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{61}{10}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{31}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{25}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{63}{10}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{34}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"416\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23446454eb9fccfe9b792aee481326e9a93c8b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50fde934b870fb9c1fc6a9092cc49004288c218e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1b7b0526168d6f1aa059eaabc8b9ec9a3421ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> is inscribed in a circle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> such that quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has an inscribed circle. If the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f1476772cd56d14a2b186ef6c1289206927f709e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+\\sqrt{b}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"41\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42df383a8680c5df86eb8a1732c37889afd52bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a,b,c)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is squarefree, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b141c3832163b865bad0556616ef5f1c1cf12bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 211\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 274\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 362\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 401\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 434$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_DMC_Mock_10_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 DMC Mock 10 Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017171133\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.068 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.082 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 660/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 23361/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:28975:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017171133 and revision id 227351. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}